WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.992
This is one of the most important ideas in the module.

00:00:02.992 --> 00:00:07.452
ON and WHERE are not interchangeable in an outer join.

00:00:07.452 --> 00:00:11.547
The ON clause defines which rows are allowed to match.

00:00:11.547 --> 00:00:15.302
The WHERE clause filters the final joined result.

00:00:15.302 --> 00:00:21.042
Suppose we LEFT JOIN patients to lab results and we only want Glucose tests.

00:00:21.042 --> 00:00:27.057
If we place the Glucose condition inside ON, we are saying: every patient should remain,

00:00:27.057 --> 00:00:30.072
but only Glucose rows are allowed to match.

00:00:30.072 --> 00:00:35.887
Patients without Glucose results still stay in the output with NULL lab fields.

00:00:35.887 --> 00:00:40.552
If we move that same condition into WHERE, the meaning changes.

00:00:40.552 --> 00:00:45.477
After the LEFT JOIN, unmatched patients have NULL in the lab test name.

00:00:45.477 --> 00:00:52.327
The condition test_name equals Glucose is not true for NULL, so those patients are removed.

00:00:52.327 --> 00:00:55.392
This issue appears in many projects.

00:00:55.392 --> 00:01:01.192
Imagine every customer should appear, but only orders from 2026 should match.

00:01:01.192 --> 00:01:07.067
If the year condition is in ON, customers with no 2026 orders remain.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:11.577
If you put the year condition in WHERE, those customers disappear.

00:01:11.577 --> 00:01:16.002
The query still runs, which is why this bug can be dangerous.

00:01:16.002 --> 00:01:20.480
Always ask whether a condition controls matching or final filtering.
